==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|tarif}}, from {{der|en|it|tariffa}}, from {{der|en|ota|تعرفه|tr=ta'rife}}, from {{der|en|fa|تعرفه|tr=ta'refe}}, from {{der|en|ar|تَعْرِفَة||tariff, rate}}, via {{der|en|he|תַּעֲרִיף|tr=tariff}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtæɹɪf/}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛɹəf/}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈtæɹəf/}}<ref>{{R:Merriam-Webster Online}}</ref>

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[system]] of [[government]]-[[impose]]d [[duties]] [[levied]] on [[import]]ed or [[export]]ed [[goods]]; a [[list]] of such duties, or the duties themselves.
# A [[schedule]] of [[rate]]s, [[fee]]s or [[price]]s.
# {{lb|en|British}} A [[sentence]] determined according to a [[scale]] of [[standard]] [[penalties]] for certain [[categories]] of [[crime]].

